      "THERESE: Well - yes. I just planned to get there a little...\nCAROL: You should go ahead.",
      "CAROL: I’m looking for a doll. She’s about- - this high and this wide and... : Let’s begin again, shall we?\nCAROL: I wonder if you might help me find this doll for my daughter.\nTHERESE: Bright Betsy. She cries.\nCAROL: Oh she does?",
      "ROBERTA WALLS: Belivet? Miss Belivet?\nROBERTA WALLS: Over here please. Now?\nTHERESE: Sorry - I’m - excuse me.\nTHERESE: Hello?",
      "CAROL: I did. And the gloves. Thank you so much. You’re a star for sending them. I just called to say - thank you, really.\nTHERESE: Of course.\nCAROL: Oh, shit - sorry. What I mean to say - Do you get a lunch hour there? - Let me take you to lunch. It’s the least I can do.",
      "CAROL: I’m so sorry to keep you waiting. I’ll have the creamed spinach over poached eggs. And a dry martini. With an olive.\nTHERESE: I’ll have the same."
    ]
